A||||11||V8 Fiero Fan||V8 Conversion Kits||||1||
Z||000000||V8 Fiero Fan||05-31-2000||12:19 PM||||I'm new to the Fiero scene, and I have seen a number of V8 Conversion Kits available.  I see that the Archie Kit is popular, but I was wondering if anyone has used the Corson Kit or the Zumalt Kit (is the Zumalt even available anymore?)<P>I would appreciate any feedback on these Kits or others.  <P>Also, does anyone on this forum know of anyone in the Detroit area with a V8 conversion?||||reg||1
Z||000001||Spyder||05-31-2000||06:40 PM||||I did the V8 Archie swap. <BR>I did tons of research.  <BR>I called and talked to a lot of people. <BR>Archie had the best price, a custom made clutch, and he was willing to talk to me and steer me to the right direction.  <BR>He also went out of his way to help me with my 328 kit car. He made me a copy of an installation video that he had and sent it to me for free.<BR>So ask around (like you just did) and do some phone calls and decided for yourself.<P>Also, on the big axle argument, you’ll hear it if you haven‘t already, I will tear up my transaxle before I will bend or mess up an axle.<P>I did talk to Corson and I liked them also, but I ended up going with V8 Archie.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||05-31-2000||08:27 PM||||Okay. let me add a touch of controversy here.<BR>I would like to find a V-8 kit that doesn't put the moving parts in the wheelwell. I don't have any problem with replacing the axles with different ones. I have seen the Zumalt stuff, but I hear he's about out of the biz. (Never returned *my* phone call, anyway.) The Corson stuff actually looks like the Zumalt stuff. PISA (Corson?) usta sell Zumalt's kit, but now they are recommending Archie. Nothing against Archie, I just won't put my pulleys outside.<BR>If I was going to buy an Archie kit, it would be to install a 4.3 V-6. <BR>Arch? Ya' listening? How bout a 4.3 kit?<BR>Vortec Archie sounds almost as cool as V-8 Archie. ||||reg||5
Z||000003||Oreif||06-01-2000||02:32 AM||||Just get the V-8's that use the cam driven water pumps and no pulleys will stick into the wheel wells. I'm not sure which motor it is (LS,LM,or LT) but I know it's one (or 2) of them.||||reg||1
Z||000004||2birds||06-01-2000||12:49 PM||||What'so bad about putting the pulleys in the wheel well?  <BR>There's a guy in my area who has been trying to put an LT1 in his 88 coupe for the last year.  He bought a kit that required new axles, I think it came from PISA, and he still had clearance problems on the front/right side of the engine.  The LT1 has the plug wires coming out under where the water pump pulley would be, and this caused clearance problems with the chassis rail on the right side.  He ended up cutting to make it fit, and then he had problems with his Getrag and numerous electrical problems, so I don't know if he ever ended up getting it on the street again.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Spyder||06-01-2000||01:07 PM||||I will be making a cover to go over my pulley in the wheel well but I haven’t heard of any one ever having any problems with it there.||||reg||1
Z||000006||batboy||06-01-2000||08:52 PM||||When I was looking to buy the Batmobile, that water pump pulley and belt running in the outer wheel well bothered me too. A year later, I don't worry a bit about it anymore. It really hasn't been a problem and since I lowered the car, it's almost totally hidden now. I have thought about making a custom cover for it like Spyder suggested.||||reg||1
Z||000007||ezsurf||06-01-2000||11:58 PM||||Spyder,<BR>Judging by your previous post, I take it you have a 4 or 5 speed manual transmission in your V-8 Archie conversion.  I was wondering if this was the stock Fiero transmission, or was it one from another car?  Also, I was wondering if the stock Fiero automatic transmission is used with Archie's conversions?  If so, do they require any modification?||||reg||5
Z||000008||batboy||06-02-2000||12:06 AM||||I have an unmodified TH125 automatic in my V8 Fiero. I plan on putting in a shift kit.||||reg||1
Z||000009||ezsurf||06-02-2000||12:15 AM||||Batboy,<BR>What conversion kit did you use?  Also, would you use this kit again or recommend someone else?||||reg||5
Z||000010||Spyder||06-02-2000||12:48 AM||||ezsurf <BR>When I was doing the V8 install in my 84 se, the Fiero with the 4 speed with the 4.10,  I decided to go with the 5 speed for the extra gear out of an 88 coupe (Isuzu) .  I always felt that I needed to shift again even with the 4 cylinder engine.  <BR>If I tear it up I will just replace it with the same or maybe a different 5 speed. <BR>But the drag racing days of mine have passed, I am more into midrange power now.<BR>So it should last longer than some.<P>When I had stock wheels and tires on it I took it for a little “spin”, it would bark every gear with authority. Other than that I haven’t pushed it yet, just an occasional drive around the block. I’m redoing the suspension right now and a paint job soon.<P>You can use a stock automatic transaxle with no modifications.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Dan86gt3.8||06-02-2000||02:48 AM||||Ok wait up a sec is corson the kit thats now on pisa's site?  I have thier old catolouge with the zumalt kit.  Also what all is necesary for the swap.  of course engine and tranny.  But how about this oil cooler, oil filter relocater, flywheel, exhaust,etc.  Which kit is the best to get, if you get the master build kit is it cheaper in the long run?  The idea still intrigues me because it is cheaper than the northstar but not by much. figure 3k for the masterbuild kit and 3k for building a good motor.  So thats 6k and design one wants what 7k for a northstar.  I am personally torn between the SBC, the northstar, and a 3.8 s/c.  But its pointless because I am a poor joblss, college student, who wont be doing any of this untill I graduate in 2-3 some odd years.  I would think that a small block would break tranny's and axles, but archie seems to realy believe that axles won't break and trannys wont if you do not abuse them.  Has he ever gone to any persons house to fix a broken axle, like he promises?  Everyone seems to like archie, although I talked to someone that says they have compliants about him.  But everyone seems to hate ace, but I think he's ok so I guess its just all in who you talk to <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">.....||||reg||1
